(foam_xyuv.ngc - a two-plane foam program with a dwell and an M1xx.)
(Drawn under GEOMETRY = "XY;UV": the XY columns make one plane at foam_z)
(and the UV columns another at foam_w. The extents, though, stay in the)
(machine frame and are unaffected by the geometry string - except for the)
(Z pair, which calc_extents replaces outright with min/max of the two)
(plane heights. Both halves of that need a program that actually moves)
(U and V independently of X and Y.)
G20 G90 G94
G0 X0 Y0 U0 V0
G1 F20 X1 Y0 U0.8 V0.1
G4 P0.05
G1 X1 Y1 U0.9 V1.2
M100 P1 Q2
G1 X0 Y1 U0.1 V1.1
G1 X0 Y0 U0 V0
G4 P0.05
M2
